ted_at":1787768311,"sha":"00bb5a0824bc02a0eadadcf9b1aa352ef17cd920","subject":"fix(notification-gates): bound cancel_gate lock acquisition with a timeout"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"efa928ff387ff70c4c520fe07c638723cbfc40908eea41c891b0e0e3f0338c65","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/commits.json","size_bytes":252},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"84db5610af09f9b1ffaa65ff676202b6ce6bca37988b19399b3858119cd2d7a6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/meta.json","size_bytes":10771},"prompt":{"digest":"e372e8e9735c583f851b3a245df47cb1fd489be15fc1857662d46e400d23c418","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":168},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"2a08fd212b70c4c009a6c0afbe96f3eacb687a24804fbfac5fb44b6b0a99c4f8","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":4173},"state":{"digest":"5e05d522b0c796cd6bc4fefb2194afad9a722930a7d8fef92ba2fb7134d3d5ef","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-ud.1","local_name":"sase-ud.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-ud","agent_clan_generation":"20260826140444","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-ud.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-ud[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Gate shells — a decision that outlives the agent that asked[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every sase gate that an agent creates becomes a named gate shell in[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that agent's family, kills its creator instead of blocking it, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]streams its approved commands' live output into ACE, owns the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]family's TALE/QUESTION/APPROVED statuses, and launches a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]configurable follow-up agent carrying the gate's typed results — [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]with gates and monitors sharing one family-shell substrate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]gate_shells.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/gate_shells.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ud[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ud/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bounded gate response lock[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]lock-timeout[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock-timeout: give file_lock an optional timeout and use it in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cancel_gate so a cancellation can never block behind an approved [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]long-running command.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The sase.shells family-shell substrate[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]shells[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shells: extract member creation, suffix allocation, handoff, settlement,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-up launch, prompt scaffolding, status pairs, and state buckets [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]out of sase.monitor into a kind-parameterized sase.shells package, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase.monitor as a facade; migrate monitor follow-ups to #fork:<family>.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate shell creation, handoff, and settlement[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-shell[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shells[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-shell: add the additive `shell` block to the v3 gate request, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]create the gate-shell family member with promotion and claim transfer, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hand off and kill the creator through .sase_gate_pending, run the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ordered settlement, short-circuit %auto, and bound pending gate shells [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with a required timeout and a reclaim chop.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust read-side gate shell rules[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-core-rs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-core-rs: add the flat gate fields to AgentMetaWire and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]DoneMarkerWire, add is_real_gate_member_record, free the runner slot for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a pending gate shell in both the Rust and Python admission copies, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extend the scanner and newest-family-shell selection.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable gate execution and live output[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-exec[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-exec: bind the executor's three streaming callbacks to the gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shell's gate.log through the shared bounded writer, add `sase gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]answer --detach` and default shell gates to it, record the running [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command's pid, and write the settle-time chat file.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate shells in ACE[/bold #D7AFFF]                                            [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold